ue of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 58% of normal in January to February and 61% in September to October. So far in 2026 March to April hit 233% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 27775 had its driest year in 1971 at 70% of normal.</p>"}
